1
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,360
Try walking away and see

2
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:24,460
floating on the Nakagawa

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,860
aiming for a certain day

4
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:31,480
when I kick a pebble

5
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,980
and my shoes fly off too

6
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,260
and onto the head of the
carpenter who was saving his money

7
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:48,460
they laughed that I was still a kid

8
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:53,580
even if I chase after energy somewhere

9
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:58,660
In Katsushika, nothing changes,
not even one yawn

10
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:02,540
the streetscape is strangely gentle

11
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:10,480
from the thermos with the pointed cap

12
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:16,800
the great stone pillar, the sunset falls

13
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:25,260
tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it

14
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,300
Hey, Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost

15
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:34,000
I only realized it because I'm such a fool

16
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,060
In October, like,

17
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,880
Chief Hanayama.

18
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,660
How are things down below?

19
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:45,120
Same as always.

20
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:47,420
I see.

21
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:53,260
Even though I was the one who had earned
the full respect of the station's officers,

22
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:02,560
it seems I've completely
disappointed my subordinates.

23
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:10,320
Patrolling in broad daylight?
No way I'm doing that.

24
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,580
Good night.

25
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:16,260
Damn it, this man is to blame!

26
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:21,660
The precinct's authority has
been trampled on by this man!

27
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,100
Damn you!

28
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:36,500
Hahaha! Serves you right!

29
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:42,260
Hey, Hanayama, it was you again, wasn't it?
We know it.

30
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:45,860
Stop handing out such cheap curses that
only land on the edge of the offering box.

31
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:49,040
Why don't you do something bigger,
you dummy?

32
00:03:53,780 --> 00:03:54,820
Hanayama-kun.

33
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:57,360
Mope, mope, heave-ho, cho.

34
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:59,720
If you don't pull yourself together,
Hanayama-kun,

35
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,520
I can't set an example for my subordinates.

36
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,340
I'm terribly sorry.

37
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:03,960
Hanayama-san.

38
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:07,340
It's a bare-bottom spanking for you!

39
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,620
Because of that man,

40
00:04:10,620 --> 00:04:12,600
my reputation is completely ruined.

41
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:14,280
Now, above all else, I must

42
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,440
teach that Ryotsu a lesson

43
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:18,280
and win back the trust and respect of
the officers of the Heavenly Police.

44
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,260
That's the plan.

45
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,980
Ryotsu-kun, would you like some tea?

46
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,420
Ryotsu is out on patrol right now, though.

47
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:32,540
Patrol? Is Ryotsu not here?

48
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:35,880
Are you a friend of Ryo-chan?

49
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:38,240
Sort of.

50
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:42,100
He's out on patrol, but knowing Ryo-chan,
who knows when he'll be back.

51
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:44,920
Please, if you like, wait in the back room.

52
00:04:48,400 --> 00:04:48,720
Thank you.

53
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:51,920
Oh my, what's the matter, sir?

54
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:55,520
It's been ages since anyone
spoke to me so kindly.

55
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:00,480
This tea is delicious.

56
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:04,020
It's cheap tea, only 200 yen for 100 grams.

57
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:10,120
Your kindness is what
brings out the tea's aroma.

58
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,840
You're too kind.

59
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:15,600
If only there were people
like you up above, too.

60
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:16,560
Up above?

61
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:16,740
Up above?

62
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:20,960
Really?

63
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,900
I'm completely broke.

64
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,720
Pachinko again, Ryo-san?

65
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:29,640
Terai, lend me money for lunch.
I'll pay you back double.

66
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:33,060
No way, Ryo-san. You've never
paid me back when you said that.

67
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:34,780
Never mind that. We have a customer.

68
00:05:35,020 --> 00:05:35,360
A customer?

69
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:40,120
That's right. It's pretty amazing, you know.

70
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:44,220
I've been known to rain divine punishment down on the mortal world,
splat, splat!

71
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:48,580
So that's why Ryo-chan shrank
down so small the other day?

72
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:51,180
It was something Uncle Hanayama did, then.

73
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:57,840
Yes, I thought I'd handed down an
extra-heavy punishment that time.

74
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:00,540
But it seems it still
wasn't enough for that man.

75
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:04,520
Ryo-chan turns even the toughest
circumstances into something positive, so...

76
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:09,480
Yes, even I have had a bit
of trouble with that man.

77
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:12,240
This time,
to deliver an even harsher lesson,

78
00:06:14,220 --> 00:06:20,600
Right. Even a divine punishment geezer like you can't do a thing without this cane,
can you?

79
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:25,860
Let's give it a quick try on Terai.

80
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:31,780
Divine punishment, instant effect!
Movement? Never mind, it's nothing.

81
00:06:33,640 --> 00:06:37,240
Yeah, this cane can only be used by old Mr. Hanayama,
after all.

82
00:06:39,140 --> 00:06:42,240
Mr. Ryotsu,
it's perfect weather for a drive.

83
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,980
Let's go tear it up in the Wangandoru.

84
00:06:43,980 --> 00:06:45,740
Divine punishment, instant effect!

85
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:52,280
New scarf...

86
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:57,460
See, Honda, you tried to slack off,
so you got what was coming to you.

87
00:06:58,700 --> 00:07:02,900
I see, so heavenly punishment doesn't
concern those who are merely good?

88
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:05,040
Did you say something?

89
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:07,200
Just talking to myself.
Don't worry about it.

90
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:11,100
But just dishing out punishment
isn't very productive, is it?

91
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:14,520
For example, doing it this way
makes money come out, or something.

92
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:16,580
One million yen! Here you go!

93
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:21,920
Awesome! This is the Uchide no Kozuchi,
the magic mallet!

94
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,960
Aw, too bad, Terai.

95
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:26,728
If you hadn't been so stingy
and lent me money earlier,

96
00:07:26,778 --> 00:07:29,040
I'd have multiplied it tenfold,
a hundredfold!

97
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,940
No way, Ryo-san.
That's counterfeiting, isn't it?

98
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,160
It even has the watermark.

99
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,600
It even feels like a real
ten-thousand-yen bill.

100
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:44,120
You! When did you take my cane?
Give it back!

101
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:47,120
Who'd give back something this handy?

102
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,040
I've claimed this cane.

103
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,220
No, Ryo-chan.

104
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:52,060
Give the cane back to Uncle.

105
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:55,480
As long as the cane's with me, it's mine.

106
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:57,540
The one standing there
can't do anything now.

107
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:58,580
He's just a useless old geezer.

108
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,440
No, Ryo-san!

109
00:08:03,560 --> 00:08:04,260
What do you think you're doing!

110
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,140
Thank you! You're sure to go to heaven!

111
00:08:07,720 --> 00:08:09,180
There, heavenly punishment!

112
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:12,240
What happened?

113
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:13,540
Are you all right?

114
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,480
Where's Ryo-chan?

115
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:16,820
Over there!

116
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:22,974
For a heavenly chief with such a grand title,
all he does is

117
00:08:23,024 --> 00:08:26,200
a simple job anyone could do with a cane!

118
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:35,740
What was it again for reversing it?

119
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,400
Right, undo the heavenly punishment!

120
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:49,300
Counterattack!

121
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:55,780
-Senpai!-Ryotsu!

122
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:56,774
Chief,

123
00:08:56,824 --> 00:09:01,200
When I was shrunk down, you really
made a plaything of me, didn't you?

124
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:08,600
-What do you think you're doing,
Ryotsu!-Please, stop!

125
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,340
It's all right. I won't crush you.

126
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:13,840
What's this?

127
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:15,940
Money!

128
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,220
Which one is it?

129
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:19,600
Damn it!

130
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:24,140
Which one?

131
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,460
The line...

132
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,080
Reeling in Ryo-chan is easy.

133
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,720
You good-for-nothing!

134
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,940
You shameless brute!

135
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:39,660
Divine punishment!

136
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,840
What's this? He's a panda!

137
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:51,860
In that form, may you feel shame
for the ugliness of your heart!

138
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:55,360
I'm heading out on patrol now,
so you're in charge.

139
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:00,820
Hey, you old goat Hanayama! Change me back!

140
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:05,460
Ryo-chan, you're so cute!

141
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:09,000
Bucha!

142
00:10:09,020 --> 00:10:10,560
Don't climb on me! It's stifling!

143
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:14,180
How am I supposed to live
like this from now on?!

144
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:16,480
Mom, Kant-san is here!

145
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:17,660
So he is!

146
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:20,680
Hey! Viewing fee is 100 yen per person!

147
00:10:21,760 --> 00:10:23,080
I'm scared, Mom!

148
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:25,680
Hey! You! Pay up!

149
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:26,640
Ryo-san!

150
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:27,780
Ow ow

151
00:10:27,900 --> 00:10:32,160
Charging an admission fee is a legitimate right,
and the people in Ueno do it too! Chief!

152
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:35,620
This is bad, this is bad,
this is bad, it's terrible!

153
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:39,400
Uncle, why are you in such a panic?

154
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:42,280
Jiri, never mind that,
hurry and change me back!

155
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:43,880
Well, that's the thing...

156
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:47,580
I lost the instructions for the magic.

157
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:49,320
That's right, it's true.

158
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:53,760
I was just using the public
restroom down the way for a moment.

159
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,100
Whoa, the cane!

160
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:10,200
What? Then what's going to happen to me?

161
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,002
Without the cane that delivered
the heavenly punishment,

162
00:11:13,052 --> 00:11:15,020
there's no way to restore
you to your original form.

163
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:16,800
Don't you dare talk such nonsense!

164
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:19,380
You expect me to spend
Ryotsu's whole life as a panda?

165
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:22,960
How am I supposed to go buy betting tickets like this?
I'd stand out too much!

166
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:27,500
Senpai! Hanayama-san didn't lose it on purpose,
you know.

167
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,040
Of course he didn't!

168
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:32,620
I'm in trouble too,
you know, without that cane.

169
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:34,640
I lost it.

170
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:36,880
Past the third traffic light,

171
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:38,480
you, Career.

172
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:39,980
Ryo-san,

173
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:40,500
senpai,

174
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,180
don't mind them, Nakagawa and Terai.

175
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:43,940
Call the health center right away.

176
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:47,140
A vicious stray panda is wandering the streets,
apparently.

177
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:48,140
But

178
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,860
I can't let something wander
around dressed like that.

179
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:51,500
Yes.

180
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:53,400
What am I supposed to do?

181
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:56,360
If I lose the Heaven Police's equipment,

182
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:58,220
I'll be dismissed in disgrace,

183
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:00,900
and I won't be able to return to Heaven.

184
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:06,760
Ryo-chan's desperate when it comes to his own interests,
so he'll surely find it.

185
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,020
Don't worry.

186
00:12:09,460 --> 00:12:10,020
Right!

187
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:14,760
Once that man has the cane,
there's no telling what he'll do this time.

188
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:19,460
I have to get the cane back from that man before he does anything,
even if it costs me my life.

189
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,220
Uncle!

190
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:47,640
What?

191
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:48,960
What is it?

192
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,800
What is this? It looks like candy.

193
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:57,220
Excuse me, excuse me, excuse me.

194
00:12:57,220 --> 00:13:00,300
It's a candy house!

195
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,340
Bandar Shabbedar!

196
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:08,940
Wow, a candy house straight
out of a picture book.

197
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,620
Is it really made of cookies?

198
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:16,380
It must be the work of
whoever picked up the cane.

199
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:18,240
But who would make something like this?

200
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,740
What on earth is that?

201
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:25,160
It's like someone turned
a toy box upside down.

202
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:30,380
I've got it! The one who took
the cane is at the kindergarten.

203
00:13:31,340 --> 00:13:33,160
Because he can't tell comics from reality!

204
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:34,480
We have to get it back quickly!

205
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,060
Let's make it small!

206
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:45,360
Now it's easier to use, right?

207
00:13:45,830 --> 00:13:48,420
Lend it to me!
I'm gonna bring out Mika's doll!

208
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:49,380
My turn next!

209
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:50,980
A panda!

210
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:53,340
I'm doing it right here after all!

211
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,120
Hey, the cane first before playing!

212
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:00,220
Where's the cane?

213
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:02,300
Let's go too!

214
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:03,460
What should we do with this?

215
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,680
Right! Let's put it away in here!

216
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,400
We'll use it again later!

217
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:11,560
I didn't come here to play! Let go!

218
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:15,160
What a nice day for golf,
isn't it, Principal?

219
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:18,660
It's a course right nearby,
so I'll be back by evening.

220
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,640
So you ordered a panda plush?

221
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:24,460
I haven't heard anything about that.

222
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,300
I'll play with you later, so wait a moment!

223
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,800
Where's the cane?

224
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:32,820
The cane?
I put it in Enchō-sensei's golf bag.

225
00:14:32,820 --> 00:14:34,440
Enchō-sensei!

226
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,340
What?

227
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:38,380
Stop that car!

228
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,280
The panda's waving at
us and catching our eyes.

229
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:43,460
What a dedicated part-timer.

230
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:45,660
I said stop!

231
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:50,080
Damn, my body's too heavy to run!

232
00:14:52,340 --> 00:14:54,240
Let's catch a taxi.

233
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:56,440
Taxi!

234
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:02,220
Damn it! Don't discriminate against animals!

235
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,100
Just in time!

236
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,500
Sei's in the sedan ahead!

237
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:09,580
I'm coming with you!

238
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:12,920
I'll get Sei back myself!

239
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:14,560
You in front, protect me!

240
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,040
You bloody old bastard!

241
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:17,960
You'll pay for this!

242
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:23,880
Never mind that, follow the taxi ahead!

243
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:35,660
Nice open course. Going for a hole-in-one?

244
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:41,240
No entry for non-users!

245
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:44,240
I only came to get my cane, let go of me!

246
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,580
Finally caught up. Alright!

247
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:51,020
There's a bear! Bear!

248
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,260
Dammit! We can't let him get there first!

249
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,140
Yes! As expected!

250
00:16:18,160 --> 00:16:20,480
Is that me too?!

251
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,300
Explain the whole story!

252
00:16:29,860 --> 00:16:35,540
Aaaah! The kangaroo, the big jump,
the third one, this too...

253
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:39,820
Me?

254
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:43,480
Grab the second one, it's a panda.
Put it to sleep with anesthesia.

255
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:49,380
Me: But kangaroos have jumping power.

256
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:50,780
Me.

257
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:52,220
Me.

258
00:17:00,280 --> 00:17:03,020
Divine punishment!
You really pulled it off, you bastard!

259
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,360
I see... sorry.

260
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:19,600
Wait!

261
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:22,280
Coming through!

262
00:17:22,280 --> 00:17:22,980
Damn it!

263
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:24,560
I messed up.

264
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,620
I should've grabbed a cab
from that slowpoke old man.

265
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:30,580
Wait up!

266
00:17:38,980 --> 00:17:41,223
Right, we lost the crow
and the old geezer too,

267
00:17:41,273 --> 00:17:45,000
at this rate we'll get caught and sent to the zoo.
We've got to do something.

268
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,500
Come on, now open today! Cabaret Pink!

269
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,280
That's the one.

270
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:51,545
Hey mister, how about tonight?

271
00:17:51,595 --> 00:17:53,720
We open at five today.

272
00:17:54,140 --> 00:17:54,920
Hey, it's fake.

273
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:56,800
You the buyer?

274
00:17:58,140 --> 00:17:58,780
The real thing?

275
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:03,220
Come on, now open today! Cabaret Pink!

276
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:05,400
Just six thousand yen per person.

277
00:18:06,640 --> 00:18:08,240
We somehow managed to pull that off

278
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:09,280
Hey, look at this.

279
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:10,620
This is pretty well made, isn't it.

280
00:18:10,620 --> 00:18:13,060
Isn't that maybe the panda
that supposedly escaped?

281
00:18:13,060 --> 00:18:14,040
No way.

282
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:15,680
You're still standing out too much.

283
00:18:18,620 --> 00:18:20,940
Hey, where are the XL-size clothes?

284
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:22,080
They're here.

285
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:24,620
So, you see, Naoko...

286
00:18:25,620 --> 00:18:49,500
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

287
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:51,500
I'm starting to get tired, I have to admit.

288
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:58,200
Looks like their nest is over there.

289
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:00,500
Once we know their stronghold,
we've got them.

290
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:07,000
Oops, my apologies.

291
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:17,840
Take me to the rooftop!

292
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:19,860
Not yet!

293
00:19:20,040 --> 00:19:20,720
Shut up!

294
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:25,380
Direct service to the ranch, sir!

295
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,620
Young people, use the stairs.

296
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:33,640
Yes.

297
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:47,020
There it is! The crow's nest!

298
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:55,180
Yes!

299
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,680
You bastard!

300
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:58,980
Quiet!

301
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:03,160
Once it's back to normal, it's ours.

302
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,500
Like hell I'll let you.

303
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:05,840
You're persistent, you bastard!

304
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:07,760
That's you we're talking about!

305
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:08,280
Let go!

306
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:23,560
Crap!

307
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,140
Our department,
after all that effort to get it back...

308
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:28,980
Whatever you say,
it's your fault for losing the cane!

309
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:30,120
What did you say?

310
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:37,380
Our department's performance this
fiscal year has deteriorated markedly,

311
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:41,920
Sorry for the intrusion.

312
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:46,680
W-what is that?

313
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:49,400
Do you think they'd mistake it for a panda?

314
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:51,040
I know that already!

315
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:55,840
You're being laid off! I'm putting it
on the agenda for the next board meeting!

316
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:57,960
Eeeeeeh!

317
00:20:57,960 --> 00:20:59,460
Eeeeeeh!

318
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:25,460
!

319
00:21:25,460 --> 00:21:26,360
Hey, what are you going to do about this?

320
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:29,540
My cane!

321
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,560
Out of the way, out of the way, out of the way,
out of the way, out of the way, out of the way, out of the way!

322
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:42,260
Is that it?

323
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,880
At this rate,
we're going to get beaten to it!

324
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:47,000
Right!

325
00:21:51,020 --> 00:21:52,740
Just one more push!

326
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:57,940
Aaaaaah!

327
00:21:57,940 --> 00:22:00,120
Aaaaaah!

328
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:21,320
I can't swim right now... Even if you force me to hand over the ball,
Honda Major...

329
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:21,900
I won't hand it over!

330
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:23,620
Hey, stop! You'll sink me too!

331
00:22:36,660 --> 00:22:37,560
Ugh, that was rough.

332
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:42,340
Hey, old man! Maybe if it were an animal,
but don't turn me into a float ring!

333
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:45,720
Looks like it's out now, senior.

334
00:22:46,520 --> 00:22:49,720
Apparently Chief Ohara was called in
by the station chief over this matter.

335
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:53,040
I wonder if Uncle Hanayama is alright?

336
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:53,960
Shut up!

337
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:56,620
Don't you dare bring that guy up!

338
00:22:57,740 --> 00:23:00,700
Maybe a panda would've been
better than a float ring after all.

339
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:03,640
Float rings only get used in summer,
after all.

340
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:07,020
But we should be able to do undercover
work without arousing suspicion.

341
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:08,440
A float-ring detective

342
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:08,960
Sounds good.

343
00:23:09,620 --> 00:23:11,160
Ryo-chan, in that case...

344
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:13,640
You lot keep deciding things
for us without even asking!

345
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:14,780
Sorry.

346
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:17,500
Everyone's matching

347
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:19,640
Uncle Hanayama.

348
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:22,700
What happened to your outfit?

349
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:29,240
Well, you see, the other day's incident was aired on a TV program called
"Heaven Police 24 Hours,"

350
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:30,980
and it became a huge hit.

351
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:34,420
So I got scouted by a
talent agency in Heaven.

352
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:39,220
Reiko-san,
I brought the famous Heaven sweets,

353
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:40,920
could you make some tea?

354
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:41,540
Yes.

355
00:23:41,540 --> 00:23:43,880
Is that so? That's great.

356
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:48,080
I'm thinking of doing talent work
alongside my police job from now on.

357
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:50,380
Wait, before that, change me back!

358
00:23:50,860 --> 00:23:54,400
Hey, take me back to Tenbatsu-ji!
Change me back, please!

359
00:23:55,340 --> 00:23:57,560
Please, change me back.

360
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:35,440
Surprise and commotion, solving puzzles together, solving problems quickly, deciding to help,
sparks of inspiration and bouncing along, bringing it all together, action that flies off!

361
00:24:36,420 --> 00:24:40,080
Above all, Smoney Power!

362
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:46,080
Gather everyone, come here,

363
00:24:46,940 --> 00:24:52,380
a dreamlike, final energy.

364
00:24:53,380 --> 00:24:56,800
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday,

365
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,680
painting the universe,
standing on the ground,

366
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:03,560
Kameari's star is coming,
the same as before!

367
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:07,120
This should be good enough, right?

368
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:08,680
Like hell it is!

369
00:25:21,820 --> 00:25:22,980
Honestly, Ryo-chan!

370
00:25:22,980 --> 00:25:25,860
Stop nagging about how short my skirt is!

371
00:25:25,860 --> 00:25:28,660
Then why don't you dress properly too,
Ryo-chan?

372
00:25:28,660 --> 00:25:31,200
Tight like that,
and you'd spot a thief right away!

373
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:33,360
Kiin! I can't run in this!

374
00:25:33,360 --> 00:25:37,260
Next time:
"Run! Reiko's Great Chase!" See you then!

